  "all_pass": false,
  "by_construction_vs_learned": {
    "by_construction": "REVOKE removes routing by a hard mask (ledger F1); replay determinism and locality-undo are consistency checks of a deterministic forward pass; provenance is trained with a routing loss (route_weight), not emergent.",
    "learned": "reading the right cell (direct, reverse, paraphrases), composing hops, answering UNKNOWN instead of hallucinating when the path is broken or the cell is revoked, refusing a routable payload whose marker is invalid (SHRED \u2014 the learned functional-forgetting result, F3), and updating the answer when the active version changes."
  },
  "claim": "A small transformer trained on re-sampled synthetic worlds reads, composes (multi-hop) and traces knowledge held in the mutable layer, and reproduces the reference semantics of update, rollback, revoke, restore and marker shredding on a fresh world, across seeds.",
